<title>LATVIA: WELFARE MINISTER WINS CONFIDENCE VOTE.</title>
<headline>WELFARE MINISTER WINS CONFIDENCE VOTE.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Parliament on Thursday supported Welfare Minister Vladimir Makarov in a confidence vote, politicians said.</p>
<p>Oposition MPs had earlier demanded Makarov leave the post over reforms to the pension law, currently being discussed by parliament.</p>
<p>Makarov earlier this week came to terms with the social and welfare issues committee of the parliament, which had also been calling for his resignation.</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 52 40</p>
